A||N||5||Mattsfiero||Somthing electrical...someone please help||||4||
Z||000000||Mattsfiero||08-08-2000||02:37 AM||||Here is the problem my interior lights fuse blew and of course I replaced it howeer when I turn the car back on it blows again. It won't stay on....I took the Dash cover off the main Dsh and tried replacing it to see if there was any Arching and couldn't find it..what I am wondering is if there is anything else I can check....Here is the full story though :<BR>okay here is the problem...the other night my wiper fuse blew so I replaced it...I got about 6 blocks from work and was stopped for having no rear running lights...I checked that fuse and sure enough it was blown so again I replaced it. Today I checked all the fuses against the Bible and replaced a couple of them however my interior lights on my Radio, heater, speedometer, Tach and odememter all went out I checked that fuse and replaced it...such leads to the existing problem.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||08-08-2000||02:49 AM||||OK I'm just thinking out loud here but I would first remove all the Bulbs from the holders. (By interior I assume you mean the ones above the mirror, The ones under the dash, and the ones by the ashtrays (and auto shifter if so equipped)) Then plug in a fuse. It can be a lower rated fuse. If it blows then the problem is before the lamps. Possibly a short near the fuse box itself.<BR>Has anything been done recently to the car electrically (added radio or alarm) ?<BR>When the wiper blew it's fuse did other fuses blow right away? I assume since you say you changed fuses out by the bible that wrong value fuses were installed previously. Were they highe ror lower ratings. If someone had a higher rated fuse in for the wiper originally the wire may have heated and melted the insulation causing a short.<BR>Just some Idea's to check out.<BR>Hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||08-08-2000||09:28 AM||||You may have two seperate problems or just one common one. The radio, wipersand gauges are all fed by the ignition switch. I don't suspect the switch is bad however you may have a wire chafing problem in the engine compartment. Check your wiring around the pulleys and make sure that it is clear. Have you had any fuse link problems before? The other item to check is the light switch it's self, this On second thought is the likely problem if the only problem is with lighting only.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mattsfiero||08-08-2000||03:24 PM||||Thank you Orief for your thoughts and I will definately try that and Indian Resto I have not had any Fuse problems yet and yes I installed a new radio About three months ago and haven't had a problem with them and yes the First three fuses blew at once ....It was fun    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks alot<BR>Matt <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f4.bmp.jpg"> <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mattsfiero (edited 08-08-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mattsfiero||08-10-2000||03:43 AM||||Okay here is the story I checked my circuits by pulling all the bulbs attached then putting a new fuse in. Well guess what it didn' blow Yeah. I then started placing the bulbs back in one at a time with the Lights on waiting to see if any of them trip the circuit and none of them did...I got to the radio wich I had completely removed the harness from and looked at the wiring to be sure there was nothing grounded and guess what I found an obscured little wire behind the center fascia exposed and covered it quickly after not finding the placement for it...(Though Now I know where it is supposed to be and will do in the morning) and pluged the radio back in and placed it bac...The fuse is still good and the lights all work. Problem solved I want to thank everyone for there advise and especially indian Resto for pointing out the radio ...Sorry If i sounded snappy I was too sure of yself...<P>Thanks again<BR>Matt<p>[This message has been edited by Mattsfiero (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||10
